course: dictionary
lesson: 8260
title: Rickets and soft bones
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rickets is a noun. It is the name of an illness that children can get. «Rickets is a bone disease caused by lack of vitamin D, making bones soft and legs bowed.» The sentence tells you what the illness does, so you can work out its meaning from the clues around it.
explain: Look at the clues. Bone disease tells you it affects bones. Soft tells you the bones bend more easily than they should. Bowed means curved, like a bow, so the legs curve outwards. Rickets is the illness that makes bones too soft and weak to hold the body straight.
explain: The sentence also tells you what can cause it: not enough vitamin D. Doctors also name sunlight and calcium. Try the swap check: put «the illness that makes bones soft» in place of rickets, and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Rickets is a disease in children that makes bones soft and weak.
fact: Rickets can make the legs bend, so they look bowed.
fact: Rickets is usually caused by not getting enough vitamin D, sunlight or calcium.
fact: Rickets was common in smoky Victorian cities, but it is now rare.
fact: Rickets can still happen today, so health lessons teach why vitamin D and sunlight matter.
exercise: «Rickets is a bone disease caused by lack of vitamin D.» What is rickets? | A type of bright sunshine | Something that makes you very hungry | *A disease that makes bones soft and weak | A kind of strong bone that never breaks
exercise: Which thing helps to prevent rickets? | *Getting enough vitamin D, sunlight and calcium | Eating lots of sugary sweets | Staying up very late every night
exercise: «...making bones soft and legs bowed.» What does bowed suggest? | *Curved outwards, like a bow | Painted bright red | Perfectly straight | Very long and thin
test: Rickets makes a child's bones what? | Very bright | *Soft and weak | Full of water | Hard as iron
test: Name one thing a child needs to avoid rickets. | Thick winter clothes all year | *Enough vitamin D | Less sleep | Too much sugar
exam: Which is the best meaning of rickets in «Rickets was common in smoky cities»? | A city street | *A bone illness in children, caused by missing vitamin D, sunlight or calcium | A cloud of smoke | A healthy meal
